Subject: [PATCH 2/7] media: qcom: camss: csid: a format, VC and DT per source pad

A CSID source pad was a copy of the sink pad: same media-bus code, same
size, and its RDI captured virtual channel N in the data type of that one
format. A sensor that multiplexes streams of different formats could not
be described.

Source pads now keep the code and size they are given, as long as the CSID
can output the code. Setting the sink still propagates to them, so a
single-stream pipeline is configured exactly as before.

Each RDI takes its virtual channel and data type from the sensor's frame
descriptor (get_frame_desc), from the entry whose stream it is set to
capture. Four driver-private controls on the CSID subdev, "RDI0 Stream" to
"RDI3 Stream", choose that stream and default to the RDI's own number. A
sensor without a frame descriptor is treated as before: virtual channel N,
data type of the pad's format.

The DT_ID that forms the CSID's internal CID is the RDI number, so two RDIs
can capture different data types of one virtual channel.
